                                                "sense_id": "208bcaa7-e1e3-3447-8e16-c78c8fb455a0",
                                                "text": "1924, W. D. Ross translator, Aristitle, Metaphysics, Book 1, Part 9, The Classical Library, Nashotah, Wisconsin, 2001.\nBut this argument, which first Anaxagoras and later Eudoxus and certain others used, is very easily upset; for it is not difficult to collect many insuperable objections to such a view."
